# backend/data/cache/ held two unrelated kinds of file under one name, and the
# blanket rule was a lie: gitignore never untracks, so 22 precomputed model
# specs and the quote cache were both committed while the directory claimed to
# be ignored. Split, on what each file actually is.
#
# TRACKED - backend/data/cache/<company_id>.json
#   Precomputed ModelSpecification per company. These are the served product, a
#   deploy reads them at boot, and they are reviewed by hand. They are build
#   artefacts that must ship, so they stay in version control. The directory is
#   called "cache" because that is where the loader looks, not because they are
#   disposable.
#
# IGNORED - backend/data/cache/market_data_cache.json
#   Live quote cache. get_company_market_data() re-fetches whenever the cached
#   fetch_date is not today, so the API heals itself on the first request of the
#   day and this file is correct within hours either way. A committed copy is
#   stale on arrival, and a daily automated PR against it collides with every
#   human PR. The refresh workflow now verifies and reports rather than
#   proposing, because there is nothing left to propose.
#
# IGNORED - backend/data/cache/ticker_index/
#   The SEC and NSE listed-universe snapshots, refetched on demand with a 24h
#   TTL. Purely derived from two public endpoints.
backend/data/cache/market_data_cache.json
backend/data/cache/ticker_index/
backend/export/excel/regenerate_target_models.py
*.db
valence.db
